# Ablation and time-to-known-structure analysis

Targets are the exhaustive-grid minima within 3.0 kcal/mol of the grid's global minimum. Budget = 400 relaxations. Times are right-censored at the budget (counted as 401).

## Paired comparisons (pooled over molecule × seed)

Δrecall > 0 and Δt < 0 favour the *variant*. 95% CI: paired bootstrap. p: Wilcoxon; Holm within metric.

| question | variant − reference | Δ final recall [95% CI] | p (Holm) | Δ steps to known global min [95% CI] | p (Holm) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Cartesian Perlin vs matched field (L=2 A) | cart-perlin@2 − cart-gauss-field@2 | -0.005 [-0.051, +0.041] | 0.714 (1) | +9.8 [-34.5, +57.0] | 0.765 (1) |
| Cartesian Perlin vs matched field (L=4 A) | cart-perlin@4 − cart-gauss-field@4 | +0.015 [-0.031, +0.066] | 0.674 (1) | -10.2 [-64.5, +45.3] | 0.79 (1) |
| Cartesian Perlin (L=2 A) vs i.i.d. | cart-perlin@2 − cart-iid | +0.001 [-0.057, +0.067] | 0.51 (1) | +10.8 [-39.1, +60.0] | 0.627 (1) |
| Cartesian correlated field vs i.i.d. | cart-gauss-field@2 − cart-iid | +0.005 [-0.052, +0.068] | 0.806 (1) | +0.9 [-58.0, +60.8] | 0.844 (1) |

